# Copy to .env and edit. Every value is optional; the defaults are in eww/config.py.
# Contact that goes into the HTTP User-Agent, e.g. a repo URL or an e-mail address (Nominatim and the
# GeoNames web service require an identifying User-Agent; M3 exit criterion 3 checks every call carries it).
EWW_CONTACT=https://github.com/giovanniliverani/weather-watch
# Where the SQLite file, the raw snapshots and the model cache live (default: ./data).
# EWW_DATA_DIR=data
# EWW_DB_PATH=data/eww.sqlite
# EWW_MODEL_DIR=data/models
# Where the structured provider log goes (default: ./logs; `eww doctor` reads it back).
# EWW_LOG_DIR=logs
# A CA bundle to verify HTTPS against. Needed only behind a proxy that inspects TLS (Zscaler and the
# like): it re-signs every connection with a root Windows trusts and Python does not, so every call
# fails with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED. Build one with certifi's roots plus the corporate root and
# point this at it, or just name it ca-bundle.pem at the repository root and it is found. See the
# TLS section of CLAUDE.md. Verification stays on.
# EWW_CA_BUNDLE=ca-bundle.pem

# ---- M3 enrichment (all optional; a missing credential skips that provider or tier with one logged warning)
# ReliefWeb reports: a pre-approved appname is mandatory since 2025-11-01 and the API answers 403
# without one. Request it here, named after your organisation, the purpose and random characters:
#   https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScR5EE_SBhweLLg_2xMCnXNbT6md4zxqIB00OL0yZWyrqX_Nw/viewform
# Deferred as of 2026-09-22; the collector is built, so filling this in is the whole switch-on.
# Terms: personal, non-commercial use.
# RELIEFWEB_APPNAME=
# GeoNames web service (tier 2 of the geocoder): a free username from https://www.geonames.org/login,
# 1,000 credits an hour and 10,000 a day; without it the geocoder goes gazetteer -> Nominatim.
# GEONAMES_USERNAME=
# Title similarity for cross-source identity: "jaccard" (default) or "embedding" (the local model, M3).
# EWW_TITLE_SIMILARITY=jaccard

# ---- M5 social (all optional; a missing credential skips that collector with one logged line)
# Bluesky app password from Settings -> Privacy and security -> App passwords. The session token is
# never written to the log. Leave both blank to skip Bluesky.
# BLUESKY_HANDLE=
# BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=
# YouTube Data API key. Create it only if the Cloud project does not ask you to enable billing.
# Do not attach a billing account and do not buy quota. Leave blank to skip YouTube.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
# Reddit stays off until the platform approves the script-app request. Then set the flag and the four
# secrets. The collector stores the permalink, title, subreddit, time and preview image, and nothing else.
# EWW_REDDIT_ENABLED=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# REDDIT_USERNAME=
# REDDIT_PASSWORD=
